---
description: How changes reach apex.org.il
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Never push to `main`. Anything merged to `main` goes live on apex.org.il within about a minute.

To ship a change:

1. Work on a branch (for example `update/homepage-text`).
2. Run `pnpm build` and fix any errors. TypeScript errors fail the build.
3. Push the branch and open a pull request. Vercel adds a preview link to the PR.
4. Check the preview on a phone, then ask the site owner to merge.

Content lives in `content/` (text, numbers, events, people). Items marked `missing(...)` or `approved: false`
block the production build until they are resolved; see `content/release.ts`.

Do not touch DNS settings or Vercel environment variables. Keep `/add-member` and `data/members.ts` working:
`/api/add-member` inserts one line into `communityMembers` right before `export const allMembers`.
